Side-chain rotamer contour grids (Top8000)
=========================================

Seventeen n-dimensional grids of rotamericity (fraction of the Top8000 distribution, in
[0, 1]) over the side-chain chi angles, one per file:

  arg, lys             4-D, 36 x 36 x 36 x 36 bins of 10 degrees on [0, 360)
  gln, met             3-D, 45 x 45 x 45 bins of 8 degrees
  glu                  3-D, 45 x 45 x 23 (chi3 on [0, 180))
  asn, his, ile, leu,  2-D, 72 x 72 bins of 5 degrees
  trp
  asp, phetyr          2-D, 72 x 36 (chi2 on [0, 180))
  cys, pro, ser, thr,  1-D, 360 bins of 1 degree
  val

These are the tables cctbx loads (mmtbx/rotamer/rotamer_eval.py, `aminoAcids`): Phe and Tyr
share `phetyr`, Leu uses the pruned `leu` table (not `leu-raw`) and Pro the 1-D chi1 table (not
`pro3d`); MSE is scored with `met`. Generated by scripts/convert_rota8000.py.

Format of <table>.bin (zlib stream; little-endian):

  b"ROT8", u8 version = 1, u8 n_dim,
  n_dim x (f64 min, f64 max, u32 n_bins, u8 wrap),
  u32 n_values, n_values x f32 (the distinct grid values, ascending),
  N x u16 index into those values for each bin, row-major with the last dimension fastest,
    written as all N low bytes followed by all N high bytes.

The encoding is lossless: every bin decodes to the same f32 that cctbx holds in its
`flex.float` lookup table (checked bin by bin against cctbx's rota8000-*.pickle caches).

